    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0245" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg175"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 326.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-08-15"><hi rendition="#italic">August
                                15,</hi> 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Complaints having been made through Mr.
                    Stuart, her Britannic Majesty’s charge d’affaires here, of the exaction of bonds
                    on merchandise exported from New York for Nassau, explanations upon the subject
                    have been requested of the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>A copy of a letter of the 9th instant, from Mr. Harney to Mr. Chase, is herewith
                    enclosed, which contains those explanations. You may, if you deem it necessary
                    or proper, communicate a transcript of the same to Earl Russell.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
